A||N||22||fierofreek2001||what to prepare for a turbo||||1||
Z||000000||fierofreek2001||07-02-2001||10:33 PM||||hey guys, i have been wanting a turbo car, thinking like a 300zx or 3000gt.. but i thought.. hey since im rebuilding the fiero gt, why not think about a turbo..    the question is, what do i have to do to prepare the engine in order to make it "turbo ready" when i get the funds to put one in?  i would like to make the engine ready , so that i wont have to do things different in the future and tear everything out again... <BR>thanks<BR>steve||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierofreek2001||07-03-2001||10:52 AM||||*bump*||||reg||1
Z||000002||West Coast Fiero||07-03-2001||10:56 AM||||if you plan to use 7 to 8 lbs of boost you dont neccessarily have to do anything to the engine, what engine are you thinking of using, or are you sticking with the 2.8?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dave Gunsul||07-03-2001||11:41 AM||||I'd like to add a couple questions to the ones West Coast asked above.<P>Are you going to rebuild your engine?<P>If not how many miles are on it currently?<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000004||00lE||07-03-2001||01:18 PM||||I would dump the 2.8 block and find a decent 3.1 shortblock.  Reason being that the 3.1's are already set up to accept a knock sensor and DIS ignition.  You will have to replace the pistons, but IMO you would need to do that anyway.  A good set of custom forged pistons with a slightly lower compresion ratio would be ideal.  Total Seal makes a great set of rings for nitrous applications that are also great for forced induction (Part # 267500001-06) You will also need to drill a hole in your oil pan just above the oil level for the turbo oil return.  Once you get everything back toghether you will need to change to a 2-bar map sensor.  You will also need a better engine managment system, but since you are now DIS capable you can use the 1227727 ECM and Turbo Grand Prix eprom.  It is already set up for the 2-bar map and will also control your turbo wastegate.  You would need to mate the engine harness from a 3.1 fwd that uses the 1227727 ECM to your existing Fiero harness, but its not very hard to do.||||reg||1
Z||000005||88formula||07-03-2001||10:06 PM||||Mechanically I would make the bottom end stronger. I would use low compression (8.0-8.5) forged pistons, SBC connecting rods, ARP rod bolts and main studs, balanced reciprocating assembly, and a high volume oil pump. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||West Coast Fiero||07-03-2001||10:20 PM||||do you plan to use a water cooled turbo?<P>I think the other responses are fron people who are really on top of it, right on||||reg||1
Z||000007||Terrybogin||07-03-2001||10:31 PM||||If you go with the DIS/727 ecm, use the aluminum heads also. The Grand Prix turbo prom will run pretty crappy with the iron head motor- I tried it, it would run, but performance was very sluggish. If you want to keep your iron heads and Fiero intake, get a '749 ecm and GMC syclone prom. The '749 is easier to mount than the '727 because the '727 is a weather proof (engine bay mounted) ecm and the case is very different while the 749 is the same diminsions as the Fiero ECM. For what it's worth, we had my son's car wired for the stock ECM, the '727 and '749- all at the same time! Within than 10 minutes, we could swap from one ECM to the other, and switch from DIS to distributer when needed for the prom we were using. Currently, it has the '749 ecm and nearly stock Syclone prom. I wanted to try running a TPI v8 ecm ('165?")mass air, but we got tired of messing with it.||||reg||1
Z||000008||fierofreek2001||07-03-2001||10:40 PM||||wow, thanks for the responses guys... as of right now im sticking with the 2.8..  it is being rebuilt at 117000 miles on it, like i was saying, i wanted to get the right parts i need for this engine now, so that i wont have to rebuild AGAIN when i have the turbo installed<BR>some of the stuff u guys are mentioning is really helpful, thanks !     ( but some of it is like reading spanish  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  )||||reg||1
