Z||000010||fierofreek2001||07-04-2001||12:59 AM||||i was just surfing the web and ran across  DESIGN ONE <A HREF="http://www.design1systems.com/turbo/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.design1systems.com/turbo/index.html</A> <P>has ANYONE got this turbo, or know anything about it?!  its not mentioning hardly any mods at all<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennockssig.jpg"> <BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI> "Unofficial Pace Car"<BR><LI> 86 Fiero GT<BR></UL>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Dave Gunsul||07-04-2001||03:03 AM||||I would suggest using forged low comp. pistons as well. TRW makes a forged piston in the stock 8.5:1 comp. PAW sells them. <A HREF="http://www.pawengineparts.com" TARGET=_blank>www.pawengineparts.com</A> <P>Make sure you use a high vol. oil pump!<P>You might also want to consider using:<BR>synthetic oil after the 3,000 mile point,<BR>an oil cooler, and an adj. fuel pressure regulator.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000012||Predator||07-04-2001||10:41 AM||||I have the Design One Systems Stage II kit. It requires no modifications to the motor other than what is required to install the turbo. No internal engine mods are required. If your engine is not a high milage engine then the kit will work. I would have the fuel injectors cleaned, and a high volume oil pump installed as you install the kit. Also, make sure your car is tuned up properly as well. If you have a manual transmission the system comes with a new exhaust. I have it, and I like it, but it is a little loud. Good Luck with whatever you choose. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||fierofreek2001||07-04-2001||11:17 AM||||predator, do u have any pics or stats on that turbo of urs? thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||fierofreek2001||07-04-2001||11:20 AM||||predator, do u have any pics or stats on that turbo of urs? thanks<BR>steve||||reg||1
Z||000015||Predator||07-04-2001||11:35 AM||||I have been meaning to take some pictures of the whole car setup. Currently Kevin at Design One is making a few changes to the EPROM to help with a lean condition I have been having under boost. I should get the chip back sometime next week. I will then have a Dyno run done, and let you know how it turns out. The stat's I currently have are under the lean condition so I don't want to post them until I get a good run. I will try and post some pics of the setup. It is a pretty big job installing the kit. It took me working by myself about two full weekends to install it. If you are like me and don't have a lot of professional tools it takes a while. A lift and such would help greatly. If you get the kit I would advise having it Dyno'ed to check your setup. Also, you will need to get a Fuel/Air guage. These are things I learned after the fact. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||fierofreek2001||07-04-2001||12:02 PM||||predator, let me know via email   steve@fierosteve.com  ...   luckily we do have an in-ground lift and lots of good tools here, my dad has been a mechanic for over 50 years.. sheeeesh thats a long time<BR>thanks<BR>steve||||reg||1
Z||000017||fierofreek2001||07-07-2001||12:33 AM||||hey guys, just had a couple more questions...<BR>first:  If the air is boosted so much, then how am i supposed to be getting more fuel to the engine?  ( im new to this )   i mean, should the ratio be the same?  a new throttle body perhaps?<BR>second: for the design one turbo, why is it that that kit for the automatic doesnt come with a new exhaust?<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennockssig.jpg"> <BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI> "Unofficial Pace Car"<BR><LI> 86 Fiero GT<BR></UL>||||reg||1
Z||000018||rogergarrison||07-07-2001||07:04 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierofreek2001:<BR><B>hey guys, just had a couple more questions...<BR>first:  If the air is boosted so much, then how am i supposed to be getting more fuel to the engine?  ( im new to this )   i mean, should the ratio be the same?  a new throttle body perhaps?<BR>second: for the design one turbo, why is it that that kit for the automatic doesnt come with a new exhaust?<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have the same system with 3.1 (basicly a stroked 2.8) 4 spd. The only major change is the crossover pipe and the oil return line into the pan. I had lots of work done to engine more for reliability than necessity. I run with about 5 pnds boost. There is quite a bit of hoses and misc other parts that are included in kit. You need some form of better ignition coil (OEM sucks) The sensor reads the amount of air going in and fuel is added by cmptr. That is up to a certain limit unless you put a higher vol fuel pump. I didnt. I did also add a hi perf oil pump. I also use Castrol Full Synthetic to take the added heat. Been all on my car and running perfect for 4 years. Oh yea, forgot to mention mine requires the 160* thermostat to run worth a s**t. 180* and 195* didnt work on mine, ran terrible.<P><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000019||fierofreek2001||07-09-2001||11:04 PM||||i recieved an email from kevin at design one systems, and he told me the stats with the turbo were as follows<BR> 0-60 in 6.0 sec and 1/4 in mid 14's @ 95mph.  <BR>do you guys really think this is worth $3000 ???   dont stock v6's do 0-60 in 7 seconds?<BR>hm..<BR>steve<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennockssig.jpg"> <BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI> "Unofficial Pace Car"<BR><LI> 86 Fiero GT<BR></UL>||||reg||1
Z||000020||Slammed Fiero||07-09-2001||11:24 PM|||| High 7's depending on the tranny used. (not auto)<P>Turbo's are great building blocks. Proper tuning and it can be quite a bit faster than 14's. Build a motor to handle more boost and it can be really fast.<P>Blow off valves<BR>Intercoolers<BR>free flow exhaust<BR>more boost<P>I had a merkur 2.3 turbo , in 20 min you could change it from a high 15 sec car to high 14 sec car.<P>More boost,I ran 18psi boost on the stock 2.3 for 2 years as a daily driver, sabb intercooler , turbocity boost valve , and a 3" downpipe made it a screamer...cheap.<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000021||rogergarrison||07-10-2001||01:07 AM|||| [QUOTE]Originally posted by fierofreek2001:<BR>[b]i recieved an email from kevin at design one systems, and he told me the stats with the turbo were as follows<BR> 0-60 in 6.0 sec and 1/4 in mid 14's @ 95mph.  <BR>do you guys really think this is worth $3000 ???   dont stock v6's do 0-60 in 7 seconds?<P>its all relative. Id bet racers would spend lots more than that to knock off a full second. Those times are prob about right for 2 identical engines, one with turbo. Mines not all that quick 0-60, its that 60-100+ that kicks ass. Mine pulls from 120 like a stock v6 pulls from 50.<P><BR>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781">  <p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 07-10-2001).]||||reg||1
